meta {
  name: Internal - Sync Employee Profile
  type: http
  seq: 90
}

post {
  url: {{hrServiceUrl}}/api/v1/internal/employees/sync
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Internal-Secret: {{internalServiceSecret}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "user_id": "{{userId}}",
    "tenant_id": "{{tenantId}}",
    "home_org_id": "{{orgId}}",
    "is_active": true,
    "date_of_joining": "2026-09-27",
    "date_of_exit": null,
    "actor_id": "{{secondUserId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Service-to-service only: identity-service calls this after Team create/edit.
  Hits hr-service DIRECTLY (not the gateway — the route is not proxied there).
  Set hrServiceUrl to hr-service's own origin, e.g. http://localhost:4007.

  Idempotent upsert of hr.employee_profiles. Returns data.outcome:
    created   — no profile existed; filed under home_org_id with date_of_joining
                (default today)
    updated   — org_id moved to home_org_id and/or is_active changed
    unchanged — already in step
    deleted   — HR soft-deleted this profile; it is not resurrected
  Joining date, code, grade and weekly off are never overwritten on an existing
  profile. A NEW profile starts with the department of the role the user holds
  in home_org_id.

  Optional exit fields (sent by identity-service on deactivate / reactivate):
    date_of_exit     "YYYY-MM-DD" sets it, null clears it (reactivation), absent
                     leaves it alone. 400 if before the joining date.
    exit_if_missing  deactivation that names no date: file today unless HR
                     already recorded one.
    exit_reason      free text (max 100), kept in metadata; dropped when the
                     exit date is cleared.

  A home-branch move re-points designation_id at the same-named designation in
  the new branch; with no match it is cleared and metadata
  .designation_needs_review is set (cleared when HR picks a designation).

  400 when home_org_id is not a branch of tenant_id, or the user has no active
  mapping there. 401 without the correct X-Internal-Secret.
}
